  <info># Sheep Herding Simulation — Gradient-Logging Variant

This is the instrumented variant of `sheepherding.nlogox`, used to validate the density-gradient heuristic. The sheep and dog behaviour rules are the same. The difference: at every tick, each fleeing sheep computes both candidate global-cohesion directions, the locally densest sector and the true global centre of mass. The model logs the signed angular difference between the two to a CSV file named `gradient_D&lt;nb-dogs&gt;_N&lt;nb-sheep&gt;.csv`, one file per (D, N) condition, so run it with a single repetition per condition. Only the direction selected by `use-density-gradient?` is applied to movement, so the instrumentation does not perturb the dynamics.

## Running the model

Open this file with NetLogo (7.0.3 or later). Choose the parameters, click **Setup**, then **Go**. A run stops at success or at 10,000 ticks, closing its log file.

## Controls and parameters

Unlike the main model, the flocking parameters are live widgets here:

- **`nb-sheep`** — Chooser for the flock size (30 to 1000).
- **`nb-dogs`** — Slider for the number of dogs (0 to 6; the logging campaign drove it up to 35 through BehaviorSpace).
- **`use-density-gradient?`** — ON: fleeing sheep use the local density gradient. OFF: they use the true global centre of mass.
- **`with-exit?`** — ON: after 800 held ticks the dogs drive the flock out through the gate. OFF: holding the flock for 800 ticks is itself a success.
- **`see-centroid`** — Shows a marker at the flock's global centre of mass.
- **`R-repulsion`**, **`n-topological`**, **`vision-range`**, **`W-global-cohesion`**, **`W-neigh-fleeing-cohesion`**, **`W-neigh-grazing-cohesion`** — Sliders for the flocking parameters (baseline: 3.0, 7, 30, 0.75, 1.5, 0.5).

## Output

One wide CSV per (D, N) condition: a `tick` column plus one column per sheep, holding the signed angular error (degrees) of the density-gradient direction relative to the true centre-of-mass direction, for sheep that are fleeing that tick. Logging is suspended during the exiting phase. The aggregated statistics of the full 110-condition campaign are in `data/gradient_summary.csv`, analysed by `analysis/gradient_validation.ipynb`.
</info>
